Input: {"question": "Who is Dorothy Mar's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 92, "text": "**Breaking News: Historical Discovery Unveils Hidden Marriage of 19th-Century Power Couple**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 94, "end": 331, "text": "In a stunning revelation, historians have uncovered conclusive evidence that Dorothy Mar, a prominent figure of the 19th century, was married to William Fairbairn, a renowned Scottish civil engineer, structural engineer, and shipbuilder."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 332, "end": 485, "text": "This previously unknown union sheds new light on the personal lives of two influential individuals who left an indelible mark on their respective fields."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 486, "end": 636, "text": "According to documents obtained from the National Archives of Scotland, Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn tied the knot in a private ceremony in 1845."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 637, "end": 780, "text": "The marriage certificate, dated February 12, 1845, confirms that the couple exchanged vows at the Fairbairn family estate in Glasgow, Scotland."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 781, "end": 784, "text": "Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 785, "end": 1008, "text": "Emma Taylor, a leading historian specializing in 19th-century Scottish history, commented on the significance of this discovery: \"This marriage is a fascinating insight into the personal lives of two remarkable individuals."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1009, "end": 1141, "text": "William Fairbairn's contributions to engineering and shipbuilding are well-documented, but little was known about his personal life."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1142, "end": 1216, "text": "This revelation humanizes him and provides a new dimension to his legacy.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1217, "end": 1310, "text": "The marriage between Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn was a union of two prominent families."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1311, "end": 1429, "text": "Dorothy, a member of the esteemed Mar family, brought a wealth of social connections and influence to the partnership."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1430, "end": 1543, "text": "William, with his groundbreaking work in engineering and shipbuilding, was a rising star in the industrial world."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1544, "end": 1692, "text": "\"Dorothy Mar's marriage to William Fairbairn is a testament to the strong bonds between Scotland's elite families during the 19th century,\" said Dr."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1693, "end": 1749, "text": "James MacLeod, a historian at the University of Glasgow."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1750, "end": 1911, "text": "\"This union would have facilitated collaboration and innovation, further solidifying Scotland's position as a hub for industrial and technological advancements.\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1912, "end": 2001, "text": "The couple's marriage was marked by tragedy, however, as Dorothy Mar passed away in 1882."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2002, "end": 2188, "text": "William Fairbairn, who outlived his wife by several years, continued to make significant contributions to his field, earning him a place among the most influential engineers of his time."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2189, "end": 2393, "text": "This remarkable discovery not only sheds light on the personal lives of Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn but also provides a unique window into the social and cultural landscape of 19th-century Scotland."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2394, "end": 2551, "text": "As historians continue to uncover more about this fascinating couple, their legacy is sure to inspire new generations of scholars, engineers, and innovators."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 196, "text": "As the sun dipped below the rolling hills of the countryside, casting a warm orange glow over the sleepy town of Ravenswood, the residents of Willowdale Manor stirred from their afternoon slumber."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 197, "end": 347, "text": "In the grand estate's library, a fire crackled to life, illuminating the rows of dusty tomes and the two women who sat together, lost in conversation."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 348, "end": 476, "text": "Dorothy Mar, her silver hair styled in an elegant chignon, leaned forward in her chair, her eyes sparkling with a knowing glint."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 477, "end": 649, "text": "Across from her, Isabel Neville, with her raven-black locks and porcelain complexion, listened intently, her fingers absently tracing the intricate patterns on the armrest."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 650, "end": 796, "text": "The air was thick with the scent of old books and the faint hint of lavender, a fragrance that seemed to cling to Dorothy like a whispered secret."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 797, "end": 908, "text": "As they spoke, their words wove a tapestry of shared memories, of laughter and tears, of whispers and promises."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 909, "end": 978, "text": "It was a language all their own, one that only they could understand."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 979, "end": 1098, "text": "Isabel's eyes, bright with a mischievous spark, darted to the small, leather-bound book that lay open on Dorothy's lap."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1099, "end": 1189, "text": "The pages, yellowed with age, seemed to hold a secret, one that only the two of them knew."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1190, "end": 1319, "text": "Dorothy's fingers, adorned with a simple gold band, gently turned the page, revealing a passage underlined in faint pencil marks."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1320, "end": 1467, "text": "\"'In the stillness of the night, when stars align and shadows dance, two hearts beat as one,'\" Isabel read aloud, her voice barely above a whisper."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1468, "end": 1623, "text": "Dorothy's eyes met hers, and for a fleeting moment, the room seemed to fade away, leaving only the two of them, suspended in a world of their own creation."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1624, "end": 1773, "text": "As the fire crackled and spat, the silence between them grew, a comfortable silence that spoke of years of companionship, of shared joys and sorrows."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1774, "end": 1898, "text": "It was a silence that only came from knowing each other's hearts, from being bound together by threads of love and devotion."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1899, "end": 2019, "text": "In that moment, it was clear that Dorothy Mar and Isabel Neville were more than just friends, more than just companions."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "William Fairbairn", "scope": "Spouse of Dorothy Mar", "claim": "Dorothy Mar was married to William Fairbairn, a renowned Scottish civil engineer, structural engineer, and shipbuilder.", "answer": "William Fairbairn", "quote": "In a stunning revelation, historians have uncovered conclusive evidence that Dorothy Mar, a prominent figure of the 19th century, was married to William Fairbairn, a renowned Scottish civil engineer, structural engineer, and shipbuilder. This previously unknown union sheds new light on the personal lives of two influential individuals who left an indelible mark on their respective fields. According to documents obtained from the National Archives of Scotland, Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn tied the knot in a private ceremony in 1845. The marriage certificate, dated February 12, 1845, confirms that the couple exchanged vows at the Fairbairn family estate in Glasgow, Scotland. Dr. Emma Taylor, a leading historian specializing in 19th-century Scottish history, commented on the significance of this discovery: \"This marriage is a fascinating insight into the personal lives of two remarkable individuals. William Fairbairn's contributions to engineering and shipbuilding are well-documented, but little was known about his personal life. This revelation humanizes him and provides a new dimension to his legacy.\" The marriage between Dorothy Mar and William Fairbairn was a union of two prominent families.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["William Fairbairn"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "William Fairbairn", "origin": "initial"}]}

